notes: >-
  The Aura license is a custom read-only license — see LICENSE in the source
  tree. Citation does not confer copying, redistribution, modification, or
  derivative-work rights. Replication of published results in academic work
  requires obtaining a separate license from the author. Quantitative claims
  should cite the proof bundle artifacts generated by `make proof-bundle`,
  especially CAA_32B_RESULTS.json and STDP_EXTERNAL_VALIDATION.json.

  There is no tagged release. Cite a commit rather than a version: the
  `version` field in pyproject.toml reads 2026.4.20 and has not tracked the
  work, which CHANGELOG.md records under "Known version drift".

  The ten theories are the ones TheoryArbitrationFramework registers — GWT,
  IIT 4.0, predictive coding, recurrent processing, higher-order thought,
  multiple drafts, attention schema, free energy, enactivism, illusionism —
  each with a role and a module, in core/consciousness/theory_arbitration.py.
